WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.830
KARIM LAKHANI: Open innovation and
crowdsourcing is all around you.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.030
When you read an article in Wikipedia,
hundreds if not thousands of people

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.980
have contributed to that article.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.880
When you use your smartphone, whether
that be an Apple device or an Android

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.200
device, the underlying software has
been developed by hundreds of thousands

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.740
of people working collectively
to create that software

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.950
and not working for these
companies like Apple or Google.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.800
When you use your computer,
and you use the internet,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.830
the underlying infrastructure
of the internet

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.620
has been developed
through open innovation.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.740
One of the most valuable
companies in the world, Apple,

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:42.860
thinks about open source and open
innovation as key to their success.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.090
Indeed, the top companies
around the world

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:51.880
have figured out how to use the wisdom
of the crowd, the wisdom of people

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.230
distributed around the world, to help
them create products and services

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.160
that we use on a daily basis.

